{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Components"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","text":"DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It keeps a copy of the graph to look vertices up through the graph’s own vertex indices, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"component(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" hashes nothing on a graph whose indices are its vertices. The copy shares"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage (copy-on-write), so making it is O(1), and later changes to the original do not affect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the result. The cost comes later: while the result is alive, the next mutation of the original"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copies the whole graph, as it would with any other copy. Drop the result, or keep only what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you need from it ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array(components)"},{"type":"text","text":"), before mutating the graph."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A component’s slice keeps the indices of the flat storage it is cut from, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"CompressedSparseRow.successors(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does: use "},{"code":"first","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", iteration or "},{"code":"Array(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"code":"[0]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because its type names the graph’s type, a result cannot be returned through an existential"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": call it from a generic function ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"some DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":") instead."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/components"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/endIndex","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/startIndex"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/component(of:)","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/component(ofIndex:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/subscript(_:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Subscripts","anchor":"Subscripts"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/Element","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/Index","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/Indices"],"generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/BidirectionalCollection-Implementations","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/Collection-Implementations","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations"